#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Usage: scripts/release-notes <tag>. Prints the GitHub release notes: the commit subjects since the
# previous v* tag, or "First release.", then how to check the binary attached to the release.
set -euo pipefail

previous=$(git tag -l 'v*' --sort=-v:refname | { grep -vxF "$1" || true; } | head -1)
if [[ -n $previous ]]; then
  git log --format='- %s' "$previous..HEAD"
else
  echo 'First release.'
fi
cat <<'NOTES'

The tarball holds a static x86_64 Linux binary. To check it before installing:

```sh
sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
gpg --verify SHA256SUMS.asc SHA256SUMS
```

The signing key is 0F7781B7A2AB98DFB83F01B5970E4326B217EC4B on keys.openpgp.org.
NOTES
